                <pb facs="0234" n="139" sameAs="frus:frus1936v04/pg139"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.01 Outer Mongolia/94: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Second Secretary of Embassy in China</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Atcheson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Nanking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1936-05-02T15:00:00+08:00">May 2, 1936—3 p.m.</date><lb/>[Received
                        May 2—10:05 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>121. I am informed by spokesman of the Foreign Office that press reports of
                    declaration of autonomy by Teh Wang are not correct and that Teh Wang has
                    telegraphed assurances to this effect.</p>
                <p>To the Department and Peiping.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Atcheson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
